If a clinician considers a chronic-opioid-therapy for a patient and the patient has a substance-use-disorder then the clinician should discuss an opioid-use-disorder-risk with the patient and should discuss an overdose-risk with the patient and should weigh an opioid-benefit against an opioid-risk for the patient and should incorporate a risk-mitigation-strategy in a management-plan with the patient.
If a clinician considers a chronic-opioid-therapy for a patient and the patient has a substance-use-disorder then the clinician may offer a naloxone-dose to the patient and may increase a patient-monitoring for the patient.
